{"content_hash": "606d26b72b24751a", "version_id": 382, "article_id": 39, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Anthropic bans cruel behavior toward its AI Claude", "title_zh": "Anthropic 禁止用户对 AI 克劳德说刻薄话", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/08/anthropic-bans-abusive-behavior-claude", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1694975949108-c4c952d3f5ac?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8YW50aHJvcGljJTIwYmFuc3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTQ5NzUwfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Lauren Mitchell on Unsplash", "author": "Lauren Mitchell", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@laurenjean?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-group-of-people-holding-signs-in-a-park-cpj1WtwnIUk?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(97, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(135, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "12a9c277b8fb"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 108, "reading_minutes": 0.5, "lead": "Anthropic makes the AI chatbot Claude. The company now says users cannot be cruel to Claude again and again without a good reason.", "lead_zh": "Anthropic 公司开发了 AI 聊天机器人克劳德。该公司现在表示，用户不能在没有正当理由的情况下反复对克劳德说刻薄话。", "preview": "The Verge first reported the new rule. A spokesperson for Anthropic did not answer questions about what counts as abusive or cruel. The comp", "preview_zh": "《The Verge》最先报道了这项新规定。Anthropic 的发言人没有回答哪些行为算作辱骂或残忍。该公司总部位于旧金山。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 372, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/39/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 45.475, "size_bytes": 276624, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 122, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@bb5aacc/content/data/versions/382.json", "paragraphs": ["The Verge first reported the new rule. A spokesperson for Anthropic did not answer questions about what counts as abusive or cruel. The company is based in San Francisco.", "The ban does not cover normal user frustration, model testing, or dark creative themes. The old policy already had some rules about abusive conduct.", "Claude can end a conversation if a user keeps being harmful. Anthropic started this feature last August. The company called it a way to protect AI welfare.", "Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei says he cannot rule out that AI may be conscious. But Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI, says he is very uncomfortable with that idea."], "paragraphs_zh": ["《The Verge》最先报道了这项新规定。Anthropic 的发言人没有回答哪些行为算作辱骂或残忍。该公司总部位于旧金山。", "这项禁令不涉及普通的用户不满、模型测试或黑暗创意主题。旧政策已经对辱骂行为有一些规定。", "如果用户持续伤害克劳德，克劳德可以结束对话。Anthropic 去年八月推出了这个功能。公司称这是保护 AI 福利的一种方式。", "Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊表示，他不能排除 AI 可能有意识。但 OpenAI 首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼表示，他对这个想法感到非常不安。"], "body": "The Verge first reported the new rule. A spokesperson for Anthropic did not answer questions about what counts as abusive or cruel. The company is based in San Francisco.\n\nThe ban does not cover normal user frustration, model testing, or dark creative themes. The old policy already had some rules about abusive conduct.\n\nClaude can end a conversation if a user keeps being harmful. Anthropic started this feature last August. The company called it a way to protect AI welfare.\n\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei says he cannot rule out that AI may be conscious. But Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI, says he is very uncomfortable with that idea.", "body_zh": "《The Verge》最先报道了这项新规定。Anthropic 的发言人没有回答哪些行为算作辱骂或残忍。该公司总部位于旧金山。\n\n这项禁令不涉及普通的用户不满、模型测试或黑暗创意主题。旧政策已经对辱骂行为有一些规定。\n\n如果用户持续伤害克劳德，克劳德可以结束对话。Anthropic 去年八月推出了这个功能。公司称这是保护 AI 福利的一种方式。\n\nAnthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊表示，他不能排除 AI 可能有意识。但 OpenAI 首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼表示，他对这个想法感到非常不安。", "text": "The Verge first reported the new rule. A spokesperson for Anthropic did not answer questions about what counts as abusive or cruel. The company is based in San Francisco. The ban does not cover normal user frustration, model testing, or dark creative themes. The old policy already had some rules about abusive conduct. Claude can end a conversation if a user keeps being harmful. Anthropic started this feature last August. The company called it a way to protect AI welfare. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei says he cannot rule out that AI may be conscious. But Sam Altman, CEO of OpenAI, says he is very uncomfortable with that idea.", "vocab": [{"word": "ban", "pos": "verb", "zh": "禁止", "note": "ban someone from doing something"}, {"word": "cruel", "pos": "adj", "zh": "残忍的", "note": "be cruel to someone"}, {"word": "abusive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "辱骂的", "note": "abusive words or behavior"}, {"word": "spokesperson", "pos": "noun", "zh": "发言人", "note": ""}, {"word": "policy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "政策，规定", "note": ""}, {"word": "feature", "pos": "noun", "zh": "功能", "note": ""}, {"word": "conscious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "有意识的", "note": ""}, {"word": "uncomfortable", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不安的，不舒服的", "note": "be uncomfortable with something"}], "title_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude", "summary_original": "A spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude\nA spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nA spokesperson for\nAnthropic\n, which is behind AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered “abusive or cruel”.\nIn an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing or “dark creative themes”.\nAnthropic’s usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct.\nThe company’s large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI’s welfare.\n“We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we’re working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,” according to its website.\nThe notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world.\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei has\nsaid\nhe cannot rule out the possibility.\nMeanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea.\n“I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,” he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times\nreported\non Anthropic leaders’ extensive conversations with religious scholars.\nExplore more on these topics\nAnthropic\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nChatbots\nDario Amodei\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T12:42:28.979686", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.263, "sm": 100, "em": 262, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 